Title: Sitter dialog: name the refusal, the numbers, and how to resume
Created: 2026-09-23
Author: sim

--- log ---
2026-09-23T14:19Z sim created

--- body ---
## Context

Author, 2026-09-23, watching a rung-3 run: the dialog sat on "Preparing the
next attachment…" for minutes, and read as a hang. The sitter was refusing
admission — `low-disk` at 16:05 (7,8 GiB free on the tmpfs holding the data
directory, floor 8 GiB), then `cpu-busy` at 16:15 (load 7,84 on 8 cores) — and
retrying only every `IDLE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS` (10 min). Ruling: "The user should
be told the issue — and how to restart after fixing it."

What the dialog shows today, read from `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js`:

- The phase line does say "Waiting: not enough disk space" / "Waiting:
  processor busy" (`phase-*` strings, ~:392).
- The document-status line contradicts it: with `state.active === null` and
  work pending it falls through to `active-preparing` whatever the phase
  (~:2712). Same class as 0791 and 0792 — the phase must decide first — and
  those two tickets did not cover the blocked phases.
- The readings that explain the refusal (free disk against the floor, load
  against the core count, free memory) are rendered by
  `describeSDTAdmission()` into `sdt-admission`, which sits in the collapsed
  technical-diagnostics layer (~:2322), not in the primary view.
- Nothing says when the sitter will look again, or that turning indexing off
  and on re-runs admission at once (the switch starts a sweep — observed in
  the same run's log: `switch {"enabled":true}` → `sweep-start`).

## Actions

1. In every phase of `SDT_BLOCKED_PHASES`, the document-status line names the
   refusal instead of "Preparing…"; `active-preparing` is reserved for a phase
   that is actually about to admit.
2. The primary view carries, for the refusing gate only: the reading, the
   threshold, and where it was measured (the directory, for disk), e.g.
   "7,8 GiB free on <dir>; needs 8 GiB."
3. It says how to resume: what to fix, that the sitter retries on its own at
   the next check (and roughly when), and that turning indexing off and on
   retries now. Verify at execution that the off/on retry is true for every
   blocked phase before the text promises it.
4. Wording through the existing `.ftl`/`sdtText` path, like its siblings.

## Test

Red first: a render test that puts the state in each blocked phase with work
pending and asserts the status line is not `active-preparing`, and that the
refusing gate's reading and threshold appear outside the diagnostics layer.

## Exit criteria

- No blocked phase shows "Preparing the next attachment…".
- The primary view names the gate, its reading and threshold, and how to
  resume, for each blocked phase.
- The render test is red on the current build and green after.

Related: 0824 (the drivers must not wait out the same refusal).
